WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.530
- [Narrator] A Pima cotton blend T-shirt

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:03.960
on Vince's site costs $85,

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.920
but the same shirt sells
for $29.99 at T.J. Maxx.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.810
So why does it cost less?

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.910
Over 10 years, the off-price retailer

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.880
has opened 263 more stores.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.060
In 2022, TJX, which owns T.J. Maxx,

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.530
Marshalls and HomeGoods,

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.620
brought in almost $50
billion in sales revenue,

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.200
more than Nordstrom's and Macy's combined.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.000
And the secret to its success,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.910
the company isn't shifting
most of its business online,

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:32.610
or using big data to figure
out what shoppers want.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.651
Instead, it's sticking to
a decades old playbook.

00:00:35.651 --> 00:00:39.662
♪ You get the max for the
a minimum minimum price ♪

00:00:39.662 --> 00:00:43.579
♪ And it's never ever the same ♪

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.340
- [Narrator] This is the
economics of T.J. Maxx.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:50.400
There are really two components
to T.J. Maxx's strategy,

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.530
the bargain, and the hunt.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:54.690
One way T.J. Maxx gets discounted goods

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:56.430
is by buying excess merchandise

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.280
and canceled orders from
other brands and retailers.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.620
Essentially, it takes advantage of surplus

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.630
and waste in the retail system.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.700
This allows the company
to sell its merchandise

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:10.050
generally around 20 to 60%
below regular retail prices.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.160
But there's a catch.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.100
- Just the fact that the
price is low is not enough.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.440
What you need is also reference price

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:19.350
because people don't know
how much things cost.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.430
- [Narrator] That's where Alex says

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:23.250
something known as the
anchoring effect comes in.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.460
At T.J. Maxx, most items have two prices,

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.790
the T.J. Maxx Price
and a comparison price.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.010
- People anchor in the regular price

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.690
and then they see

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:36.630
exactly how much of a
deal they're getting.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:39.180
And this way they really
understand what the value is

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.040
that T.J. Maxx provides to them.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:42.840
- [Narrator] Take these rag &amp; bone shorts.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.570
A T.J. Maxx in Manhattan
sold them for about $40

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:49.560
with a comparison price of
$50, that's a 20% discount.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.530
But the original price tag
happened to be on these shorts

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.800
and it lists the price as $195.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.410
That would be around an 80% discount.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:01.320
And that comparison price
is really just an estimate.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.970
On T.J. Maxx's website,

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.347
there's a message next to the
comparison price that says

00:02:05.347 --> 00:02:08.550
"These prices are references
to regular retail prices.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.680
Where identical items are not available,

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.630
we compare to products of a similar type,

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.340
quality and style."

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.230
These price tags aren't the only way

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.090
T.J. Maxx helps customers feel

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.637
like they're getting a bargain.

00:02:19.637 --> 00:02:23.607
- You got the whole
positioning of T.J. Maxx is

00:02:23.607 --> 00:02:27.270
that we give you brand names for less.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.010
And the reason why it's important is

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.390
because very often when you see low price

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.210
you think it's low price

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.340
because the quality of the product is low.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.710
- [Narrator] But if the customer
knows and trusts the brand

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:39.210
then they won't assume the price is low

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:40.860
because it's a bad product.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.600
Instead, Alex says they'll attribute it

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.600
to T.J. Maxx's ability
to get discounted goods.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.820
And because people often
expect name brand items

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:51.390
to be more expensive, the
brand itself acts as an anchor.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.190
- Emphasizing the fact that

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:57.840
as a customer you're getting a
deal, makes people feel good.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.250
It's not only I'm getting a low price

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:01.620
but I'm actually getting a deal,

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.590
which makes people feel
good about themselves,

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:06.570
that they're smart shoppers.

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:08.280
- [Narrator] T.J. Maxx
says it gets its goods

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.230
from about 21,000 vendors

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.960
and the inventory in its
stores is constantly turning.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:16.710
- So as a result, people
tend to go more often

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.060
to this type of stores

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.390
and also spend a little
bit more time in the store

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:23.070
in search of something.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:24.180
- [Narrator] Across its companies

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.730
TJX employs more than 1200 buyers

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.470
that each control millions of dollars

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.690
and has authority to
cut deals on the spot.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:33.360
- As a buyer for T.J. Maxx,
I'm always on the hunt.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.520
- Let's say you have a bathing suit brand

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.400
and it's right before Memorial Day weekend

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.170
and they're stuck with
extra bathing suits,

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:43.410
so that's when T.J. Maxx
buyers show up at the showroom.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.630
You know, they can cut
a deal right on the spot

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.210
and they can get it to
their stores within a week.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:49.650
- [Narrator] Department
stores, on the other hand,

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:50.880
can take weeks to review

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.740
and approve orders from their buyers.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:55.260
So T.J. Maxx buys the merchandise quickly

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.570
and gets it into the store just as fast.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.810
- They have a saying internally
"Door to floor in 24,"

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.090
meaning that any merchandise that shows up

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:03.960
at a store in the morning

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:06.810
has to be on the sales floor
by the end of that day.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:07.860
- [Narrator] To ensure speed,

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.660
merchandise often arrives at stores

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.090
already on racks that
employees wheel off trucks

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.010
and move straight onto the sales floor.

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:15.300
And once it's there,

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.100
all the merchandise is
laid out differently

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.450
than other retailers too.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:21.330
Helping to create that
treasure hunt experience.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:23.940
While most department
stores group items by brand

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:26.820
T.J. Maxx organizes its inventory by type.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.290
This means that different brands

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:30.870
can end up next to each
other on the same racks.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.600
And since T.J. Maxx doesn't
have walls dividing sections

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.310
of the stores or brands,

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:36.990
it can easily reconfigure the layout

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.000
based on changing inventory.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.950
Seeing all the products
and changing layout

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:42.480
can encourage impulse buying.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.640
Shoppers know that if they
see something they like

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:45.960
they need to buy it now.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.610
If they wait, it may be sold out

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:49.350
or hard to find when they come back.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:54.030
- Once you take it home, things
are changing dramatically

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:56.400
because now you are not buying something

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.780
you are giving up something.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.130
Lots of research has shown

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:03.840
that giving up something is
more difficult than acquiring.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.870
You are willing to pay more

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:10.500
not to give up something
than to buy something.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:11.910
- [Narrator] Retailers
struggled through the rise

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.560
of E-commerce in the pandemic,

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:16.770
and while TJX's off-price
retailers still took a hit,

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:17.970
they have bounced back.

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:22.170
In 2021, TJX had the highest
sales in the company's history.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:24.840
A record it then beat the following year.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.007
And it's not because T.J. Maxx

00:05:26.007 --> 00:05:28.290
and the other off-price retailers adapted,

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:30.360
but rather because they never drifted away

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:31.710
from their core strategy.

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:33.810
- T.J. Maxx tends to perform pretty well

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:35.040
in an economic downturn

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.850
because that's when customers
tend to be bargain conscious

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:42.542
and, you know, they offer
really good value for the money.

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:45.125
(quirky music)

